; lang.xon -- what this bundle is.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every manifest
; in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon). An unknown form is a loud
; error, never a silent skip.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a requirement
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (requires-lang "NAME" ["V"]) another lang this one is written on top
;                               of, optionally at an exact version
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "ash")

; Helium plus the two modules ash imports. ash forks, execs, dup2s and opens
; files, but that needs one module -- x/sys/posix, imported by name in
; ash/prims.x -- not the whole radon library set (the numeric tower, regex, the
; compile pipeline), none of which a shell uses. The import in prims.x makes an
; unbound `Sys` fail at acquisition rather than at the first pipeline.
(dialect he)

; The x-lang release this bundle is built and tested against; CI compares it
; for equality. v0.15.0 or later is required, not merely paired with: this
; bundle names the base types through the door that release added,
; `(Type named INTEGER)`, where it read type/convert.x's private handles
; before. On anything earlier this bundle does not run.

(requires-release "v0.15.0")

(entry "run.x")
